  "caption": "A heat pump doesn't make heat. It moves it.\n\nHeat naturally flows from warm to cold. A heat pump pushes it the other way, like a pump pushing water uphill.\n\nHow? A liquid inside soaks up heat as it boils, then gives it off as it turns back to liquid. Round and round.\n\nThe payoff: moving heat takes far less energy than making it, so you get 2 to 4 units of heat for each unit of electricity.\n\nSource: Waypoint — How Heat Pumps Work\n\nSave this for your next curiosity rabbit hole.\n\nFollow @waypoint.daily for two ideas worth knowing, every day.",
